# Federal Manpower Portal — project flow

## How we work
- Build **one step at a time**. Finish a step, summarize what changed, wait for OK before the next.
- Keep code **simple and readable**. No hidden magic, no unused fields “for later”.
- Prefer clear names over clever abstractions. User must be able to change anything easily.
- Scope is flexible: drop or simplify features when the user says so. Update this rule if domain terms change.
- **No AI-flavored comments** — no “This component handles…”, “Fetch the data”, “TODO: implement”, or narrating obvious code. Comment only when a non-obvious business rule needs a short note. Prefer clear names so comments are rarely needed.

## Stack
- Laravel 12 + **Livewire 4** + Alpine
- UI: `public/css/portal.css` + Google Fonts / Alpine / Livewire CDN assets — **no Vite, no `npm run dev`, no rebuild on change** (same style as DIG)
- Do not add `@vite` to layouts. Edit CSS in `public/css/portal.css` directly.
- Patterns: follow `D:\laravel\DIG_Software_management` (Livewire panels, Support classes, custom permissions)
- Private client files: `storage/app/private/...` only — never public disk

## Client documents (security — top priority)
- **Never** use the `public` disk for client docs or photos
- **Never** `storage:link` client files into `public/`
- **Always** download/view through a protected auth + permission route
- Store only relative paths in DB (e.g. `clients/{id}/passport_copy.pdf`) — never public URLs
- On download: check login, clients permission, row belongs to that client, path stays under `clients/{id}/` (block `..`)
- Upload: whitelist mime/extensions + max size from `config/portal.php` (`client_files`)
- JPG/PNG uploads are auto-compressed after temp upload to stay under `client_files.max_kilobytes` (silent). PDFs are not auto-compressed.
- Suggested limit: **5 MB** per stored file (pdf/jpg/jpeg/png) — enough for scans, sane with many clients
- Livewire temp upload max is higher (25 MB) so large phone photos can arrive before compress
- `client_documents`: store a row only when a file is uploaded **or** marked N/A — skip empty checklist items

## Domain (plain language)
| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Client | Job-seeker / applicant (not employer) |
| Company | Overseas employer **or** university (`employer` / `university`) |
| Care Off | Person/company who referred or submitted the case (optional) |
| Process status | Stage master (Applied, Visa applied, etc.) |
| Overall status | `active` / `inactive` on each client |
| Direct vs referred | No Care Off vs linked Care Off |

## Module layout
- **Operations** holds all masters in one place: Care Offs, Companies, Universities, Countries, Trades, Process Statuses
- Care Offs is **not** a separate top-level module
- Company type: employers under Companies, universities under Universities (same `companies` table, `type` column)

## Delivery phases
- **Phase 1 (demo):** Complete operational product — Clients, portal/QR, visitors, HR, polish.
- **Phase 2 (after initial payment):** Accounts (methods, ledgers, reports) and Excel import (last). Do not build these in the demo go.

